### 2. 🟡 Intent Router — [router.py](file:///d:/MarketMinds/marketminds-chatbot/backend/app/chatbot/router.py) (STATIC KEYWORD MATCHING)

| Current | Problem |
|---------|---------|
| Hardcoded keyword lists (`"price"`, `"report"`, etc.) | Misses paraphrased queries, typos, or nuanced intent |
| `FINANCIAL_ANALYSIS` route exists but is **never handled** in [response_builder.py](file:///d:/MarketMinds/marketminds-chatbot/backend/app/chatbot/response_builder.py) | Dead code — falls through to GENERAL |
| **Bug:** Lines 9-10 execute `llm.generate(prompt)` at module import time | Crashes on startup or produces side effects |

#### ✅ How to Make Dynamic

```python
# Option A: LLM-based intent classification
class LLMQueryRouter:
    def __init__(self, llm_client):
        self.llm = llm_client
    
    def route(self, question: str) -> QueryType:
        classification_prompt = f"""Classify this financial question into exactly one category:
- LIVE_MARKET: Needs real-time stock prices/market data
- DOCUMENT: Needs to search uploaded reports/documents
- FINANCIAL_ANALYSIS: Needs ratio analysis, valuation, fundamentals
- GENERAL: General financial knowledge question

Question: "{question}"
Category:"""
        result = self.llm.generate(classification_prompt).strip().upper()
        return QueryType[result] if result in QueryType.__members__ else QueryType.GENERAL

# Option B: Zero-shot classifier (local, no LLM calls)
from transformers import pipeline
classifier = pipeline("zero-shot-classification", model="facebook/bart-large-mnli")
```

> [!WARNING]
> **Bug Fix Needed:** Remove lines 5, 6, 9, 10 in [router.py](file:///d:/MarketMinds/marketminds-chatbot/backend/app/chatbot/router.py) — they import [prompt](file:///d:/MarketMinds/marketminds-chatbot/backend/app/llm/prompt_templates.py#37-55) from `typer` (wrong library!) and execute `llm.generate(prompt)` at **module load time**, which will either crash or produce unwanted behavior.

