### 3. 🟡 LLM Client — [llm_client.py](file:///d:/MarketMinds/marketminds-chatbot/backend/app/llm/llm_client.py) (PARTIALLY DYNAMIC)

| Current | Problem |
|---------|---------|
| Ollama uses `subprocess.run()` for each call | Extremely slow — spawns a new process per request |
| [GeminiLLMClient](file:///d:/MarketMinds/marketminds-chatbot/backend/app/llm/llm_client.py#12-23) exists but doesn't extend [LLMClient](file:///d:/MarketMinds/marketminds-chatbot/backend/app/llm/llm_client.py#24-43) | Inconsistent interface |
| Import uses `from app.config` (line 66) vs `from backend.app.config` elsewhere | **Import error** depending on how the app is run |
| [get_llm_client()](file:///d:/MarketMinds/marketminds-chatbot/backend/app/llm/llm_client.py#68-73) doesn't pass `model_name` | Incompatible with `LLMClient.__init__` signature |

#### ✅ How to Make Dynamic

```python
# Use Ollama's HTTP API instead of subprocess
import requests

class OllamaLLMClient(LLMClient):
    def __init__(self, model_name="mistral", base_url="http://localhost:11434"):
        super().__init__(model_name)
        self.base_url = base_url
    
    def generate(self, prompt: str, context=None) -> str:
        response = requests.post(f"{self.base_url}/api/generate", json={
            "model": self.model_name,
            "prompt": prompt,
            "stream": False
        })
        return response.json()["response"]

# Fix GeminiLLMClient to extend the base class
class GeminiLLMClient(LLMClient):
    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__(model_name=GEMINI_MODEL)
        genai.configure(api_key=GEMINI_API_KEY)
        self.model = genai.GenerativeModel(GEMINI_MODEL)
    
    def generate(self, prompt: str, context=None) -> str:
        response = self.model.generate_content(prompt)
        return response.text
```

