### 4. 🟡 Response Builder — [response_builder.py](file:///d:/MarketMinds/marketminds-chatbot/backend/app/chatbot/response_builder.py) (PARTIALLY DYNAMIC)

| Current | Problem |
|---------|---------|
| Hardcoded demo fallback docs (lines 56-61) | Always injects 3 Apple-specific sentences into every session |
| `FINANCIAL_ANALYSIS` query type is unhandled | Falls through to plain LLM, no data enrichment |
| No streaming support | User sees nothing until full response is generated |
| No conversation history / memory | Each query is independent, no follow-up capability |

#### ✅ How to Make Dynamic

| Improvement | Implementation |
|-------------|----------------|
| Remove demo docs | Delete lines 56-61; let real documents populate the store |
| Handle `FINANCIAL_ANALYSIS` | Fetch fundamentals via `yfinance` (P/E, revenue, etc.) + RAG context, combine in prompt |
| Add streaming | Use FastAPI `StreamingResponse` + Ollama streaming API |
| Add conversation memory | Maintain a session-level `chat_history: List[dict]` and include in LLM prompt |
| **Hybrid queries** | When route is ambiguous, fetch **both** market data AND documents, merge context |

