### 5. 🟡 Financial API — [financial_api.py](file:///d:/MarketMinds/marketminds-chatbot/backend/app/data_sources/financial_api.py) (FUNCTIONAL BUT LIMITED)

| Current | Problem |
|---------|---------|
| Only fetches current stock price | No historical data, no fundamentals, no financial ratios |
| Currency is hardcoded to `"USD"` | Wrong for NSE (₹) and European stocks (€, £, CHF) |
| [TickerResolver](file:///d:/MarketMinds/marketminds-chatbot/backend/app/data_sources/financial_api.py#11-43) uses exact substring match | "apple" matches but "Apple Inc" or "AAPL" as text won't |

#### ✅ How to Make Dynamic

```python
class MarketDataClient:
    def get_stock_price(self, ticker: str) -> dict:
        stock = yf.Ticker(ticker)
        info = stock.info
        data = stock.history(period="1d")
        return {
            "ticker": ticker,
            "price": round(float(data.iloc[-1]["Close"]), 2),
            "currency": info.get("currency", "USD"),  # Dynamic currency!
            "timestamp": datetime.utcnow().isoformat() + "Z",
        }
    
    def get_fundamentals(self, ticker: str) -> dict:
        """NEW: Get key financial metrics."""
        info = yf.Ticker(ticker).info
        return {
            "pe_ratio": info.get("trailingPE"),
            "market_cap": info.get("marketCap"),
            "revenue": info.get("totalRevenue"),
            "profit_margin": info.get("profitMargins"),
            "52w_high": info.get("fiftyTwoWeekHigh"),
            "52w_low": info.get("fiftyTwoWeekLow"),
            "dividend_yield": info.get("dividendYield"),
        }
    
    def get_historical(self, ticker: str, period="1mo") -> list:
        """NEW: Get historical price data for charts."""
        data = yf.Ticker(ticker).history(period=period)
        return [{"date": d.isoformat(), "close": round(c, 2)} 
                for d, c in zip(data.index, data["Close"])]
```

